# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Cairn: what must never be committed.
#
# Rule two of the product is "nothing leaves the machine." In a public repo that
# rule has teeth only if the ignore list has teeth. Everything below is either
# user content, derived user content, or a local secret. None of it belongs in
# version control, and none of it belongs on a remote.
#
# This is an allow-nothing list for data, not a tidy-up list. If you are adding
# an exception here, stop and be sure.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- user content and everything derived from it ---------------------------
sources/            # documents the user deliberately saved
vault/              # converted markdown of those documents
*.db                # cairn.db and any sibling database
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
benchmarks.csv      # local speed log; metrics only, but it is machine-local
gates.txt           # local gate output
_ingest_failures.log

# --- transfer artifacts from the pre-git working method --------------------
*.zip
cargo*/
backup-*/

# --- local tooling and machine-specific config -----------------------------
.claude/
.mcp.json
.env
.env.*
*.local.json

# --- python ----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# --- editors and operating systems -----------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
